{
  "analysis": "The BPE tokenizer works (correctly decodes tokens back to text), but the model produces degenerate output ("hehehe..."). Two key issues remain: (1) the tokenizer splits spaces into separate tokens (token 32) instead of including them with the following word as GPT-2 BPE requires, and (2) the model layout/configuration still needs verification. I need fix the tokenizer and systematically test model configurations with correct tokenization.",
  "plan": "Write a compact test program with fixed BPE tokenization (include leading spaces with words, use byte-level encoding) that tests 4 model configurations: wte-first creation-order, blocks-first alphabetical, each with trans=0 and trans=1, all with ga=1. For each config, print top-3 predictions for 'The' and generate 10 tokens from 'The quick brown fox' with correct tokenization.",
